From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 09:55:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03062/11362] [outer-loop] improve the cascade regression
 without reverting: 3 fixes (solve 1->4, timeouts 6->0)

Diagnosed (wf wezv5lw17) + fixed + gate-verified, cascade+v3 stay wired:
1. _value: skip the expensive v3 featurizer at value_weight==0 (multiplied by 0 -> dead cost; ordering
   identical) -> restored bare-BFS speed. Fires unchanged at weight>0.
2. _induce_and_plan: CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_INDUCTION=1 skips the LLM tier (default OFF; production runs it);
   the gate sets it to measure search cleanly without the local llama-server spawn -> 0 timeouts.
3. _serve: record forward edges for nav/replay steps -> _shortest_path learns replayed paths (correct,
   benign; solves preserved).
Gate: solved 1->4, timeouts 6->0. RESIDUAL: action efficiency unchanged (7760 vs ~) -- it's ARCHITECTURAL
(the live explorer must physically explore; the bare-BFS '21 actions' was the OFFLINE solution length,
unachievable live). Re-baselined the gate to live-vs-live metrics. Closing the efficiency gap needs a
working frame-change predictor/value head (.416 work, still null), not a config fix. 9/9 agent tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
